{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"No. Naming a principal underwriter satisfies a legal and operational role; it does not itself assure a dedicated sales force, marketing effort, or asset gathering.\n\nThe underwriter typically enters into distribution arrangements, handles or oversees offering and order-processing functions, and may make required filings. The prospectus and distribution agreement matter: an ETF may be offered on a best-efforts basis, with no obligation to sell any specified amount.\n\nMarketing support, wholesaling, and access to broker-dealers, platforms, or registered investment advisers may be separately contracted—or included in a particular platform’s package. Scope, fees, and actual effort vary. Even intermediary access is not guaranteed shelf placement, recommendations, or sales.\n\nSo assess the specific trust-series documents and service agreements, including who provides distribution, marketing, and intermediary access, and what obligations they undertake."}}
